From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:46:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: stub write() signature mismatch and fsync() absence in NotificationService.cpp

Update 35b (fixing the round-35 CLANGARM64 NotificationService.cpp
2-error block at [8293/8564], surfaced via UnifiedSource-UIProcess-36.cpp):

NotificationService.cpp:79 fails with type mismatch: MinGW-w64 <io.h>
declares write() as 'int write(int, const void*, unsigned int)' (matching
MSVCRT's _write shape: the size argument is 32-bit unsigned on Windows),
while the file-level function-pointer alias expects
'ssize_t (*)(int, const void*, size_t)' with a 64-bit size_t on x86_64.

NotificationService.cpp:104 fails with 'use of undeclared identifier fsync':
fsync() is POSIX and is not declared by MinGW-w64's <unistd.h> / <io.h>
(MSVCRT's file-flush entry point is _commit()).

Fix: replace the file-scope write-alias with a small static wrapper on
Windows that calls _write() with the size narrowed to unsigned. For
flush(), use _commit() on Windows. _commit() takes an int file descriptor
(matching m_fd.value()) and forces the CRT's internal buffer to be written
to the OS; it is the documented MSVCRT equivalent of POSIX fsync().

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces both errors against a
synthesized MSYS2 CLANGARM64 configuration. Post-patch source compiles
cleanly: _write and _commit resolve through <unistd.h> -> <io.h>.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp
index 5c8e7d2..a1b2c3d 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp	2026-07-24 08:02:56.013829500 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp	2026-10-14 10:42:29.118412959 +0000
@@ -76,7 +76,16 @@
 static const Seconds s_dbusCallTimeout = 20_ms;
 
 // Alias to avoid conflicting with write() below.
+#if OS(WINDOWS)
+// MinGW: write() signature uses unsigned int for the size argument, not size_t;
+// wrap it to keep the (int, const void*, size_t) shape downstream consumers expect.
+static ssize_t writeToFD(int fd, const void* buffer, size_t size)
+{
+    return _write(fd, buffer, static_cast<unsigned>(size));
+}
+#else
 ssize_t (*writeToFD)(int, const void*, size_t) = write;
+#endif
 
 // Simple stream that writes to an fd.
 class FileDescriptorWriteStream : public SkWStream {
@@ -101,7 +110,13 @@
 
     void flush() final
     {
+#if OS(WINDOWS)
+        // MinGW: fsync() is POSIX; _commit() is the MSVCRT equivalent that flushes
+        // the file's buffers from the CRT internal buffer to the OS.
+        _commit(m_fd.value());
+#else
         fsync(m_fd.value());
+#endif
     };
 
     size_t bytesWritten() const final
